Usage: stat [OPTION]... FILE...

Display file or file system status.

OPTIONS:
  -L, --dereference  follow symbolic links
  -f, --file-system  display file system status instead of file status
  -c, --format ARG   use the specified FORMAT instead of the default
  -t, --terse        print the information in terse form
      --printf ARG   like --format, but interpret backslash escapes
      --cached ARG   use cached attribute data WHEN (hint only; always fresh on
                     Windows)
      --help         display this help and exit
  -V, --version      output version information and exit

EXIT STATUS:
  0  if OK,
  1  if minor problems,
  2  if serious trouble.

WinuxCmd is a Windows implementation of GNU CoreUtils for Linux-Windows developers and AI coding assistants.
